      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Data collections\"\n",
        "aliases: \n",
        "  - collections.html\n",
        "format:\n",
        "  html:\n",
        "    code-fold: true\n",
        "jupyter: python3\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "In the Earth Observation domain, different terms are used to describe EO data(sets). In openEO, it is referred to as a \"Collection\". Thus, a collection is a sequence of granules sharing the same product specification. It typically corresponds to the series of products derived from data acquired by a sensor on board of a satellite and having the same mode of operation. \n",
        "\n",
        "In openEO, a back-end offers a set of collections to be processed.  A user can load (a subset of) a collection using the `load_collection` process, which returns a raster data cube. \n",
        "\n",
        "The following are the list of data collections available currently in the Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem backend through openEO."
      ],
      "id": "da3a6f71"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "#| output: false\n",
        "import openeo\n",
        "connection = openeo.connect(\"openeofed.dataspace.copernicus.eu\")"
      ],
      "id": "3e6783a5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "connection.list_collections()"
      ],
      "id": "eb5e83f4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    }
